he polls so yeah what about this  message what about the message of undo  the Trump tax cuts I think that it's bad  number one because you don't want to  call them the Trump tax cuts because in  the long term they're actually tax  increases for some people because in the  short term they're disproportionately  cuts for the very rich but by saying  repeal the tax cuts you're really  campaigning on  taxes and even if that's what you have  to do even if that's the right thing to  do even if it's just a return to a prior  tax rate right it's not really raising  them it's just going back to a prior  level the optics of it aren't gonna be  good and it's way easier for Republicans  to attack Democrats if they say repeal  the Trump tax cuts or the Trump tax  fiasco or whatever Medicare for all is a  much more positive message and that's  really what I think is a key element of  how Democrats should campaign for 2018  and 2020 it has to be a positive message  so whether or not you believe Obama's  hope and change was BS and many of you  believe it was total BS and in some ways  it was total BS there were changes but  there was also sort of a reconfirmation  or a strengthening or or of a  maintaining of the neoliberal status quo  put that aside for a second it was a  positive message it was a message that  inspired people to go out and vote for  something good Bush ran a disastrous  first term and in 2004 not being Bush  did not work for John Kerry you could  say well hold on a second irregularities  in Ohio maybe it did maybe didn't put  that aside it wasn't clearly an  overwhelming win for John Kerry and  Bush's approval rating was a disaster  and being not Bush didn't work then it  likely will not work against Trump and I  think that that's why whatever the  message is it has to be a positive  message rather than a we are not Trump  message because historically that tends  not to work ok one more idea yeah free  public college education is it too out  there for most people